{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want","id":1422370,"title":"What books do you want?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-06T20:38:44-08:00","id":1422370,"title":"What books do you want?","content":"Know, or at least expected books, for the V5 line include; Cults of the Blood Gods, the Player's Handbook, Forbidden Faiths, Olsen's Standard Book of British Birds, Children of the Blood and probably Sabbat.<br /> <br /> But what books do you want to see released? What subject matters do you want covered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T21:04:05-08:00","id":1422371,"title":"","content":"I want the Players Guide next.<br /> <br /> I want a Sabbat book.<br /> <br /> I want a Second Inquisition book.<br /> <br /> I want an Elders book.<br /> <br /> Oh and if I could order any, I'd want a Chronicle book for THE FALL OF VIENNA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T21:09:17-08:00","id":1422372,"title":"","content":"Announced - Cult of the Blood Gods, Player's Guide, Trail of Ash and Bone, Second Inquisition.<br /> Unannounced - Ashira, Lore/Scenario book covering major events in V5 (Taking Mexico City, Fall of Viena, Convention of Prague, Ministry/Banu Haqim meeting with the Camarilla)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T21:09:30-08:00","id":1422373,"title":"","content":"A book about obscure bloodlibes would be mighty kind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T21:34:19-08:00","id":1422374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1422371#post1422371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want the Players Guide next.<br /> <br /> I want a Sabbat book.<br /> <br /> I want a Second Inquisition book.<br /> <br /> I want an Elders book.<br /> <br /> Oh and if I could order any, I'd want a Chronicle book for THE FALL OF VIENNA.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is almost exactly what I want, plus a real blood magic book with proper paths and not the limited blood sorcery/quietus stuff. Maybe it could fit in the Player's Guide, though.<br /> <br /> I can also excuse some of the slowness to the change in leadership and the pandemic, but back in the day they used to release multiple books a year, and that was back when they all had to be printed in decent size runs. But it's just been a slow trickle of new material. Come on guys, this work has gotten easier with telecommunications, photoshop/gimp and other tech advancements. My #1 complaint about switching to V5 from V20 is the lack of material, options and diversity available in the older stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T21:51:12-08:00","id":1422376,"title":"","content":"Not counting the ones slotted to come out already:<br /> <br /> Elders<br /> Book of Rituals - Stuff for Blood Sorcery, Necromancy/Oblivion, and Protean if I understand how they intend to do <b>Vicissitude</b> correctly.<br /> Sabat would be interesting, but not a priority.<br /> Salubri<br /> <br /> Pipe Dream: A fixed Kindred of the East. Maybe call it Vampires of the East or something. I know its not going to happen but I would greatly enjoy seeing the Wan Kuei updated and fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T01:15:14-08:00","id":1422395,"title":"","content":"A new edition of Dark Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T01:38:01-08:00","id":1422396,"title":"","content":"Vampire: the Masquerade. 30th Aniversary edition. <br /> <br /> Less a revised copy-paste, with more care to choose the best from V1,V2, Revised and v20. <br /> <br /> And use 'take half' for damage and soak to speed up combat already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T05:33:17-08:00","id":1422413,"title":"","content":"I'm eager for VtM V6<br /> <br /> or a fan edition like Pathfinder did for DnD<br /> <br /> they can nuke the sabat for all I care, I'm done waiting,<br /> I just hope they finally retcon all the dumb lore and start anew,<br /> and no more catering for LARP","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 11-07-2020, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T05:44:47-08:00","id":1422414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1422371#post1422371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want the Players Guide next.<br /> <br /> I want a Sabbat book.<br /> <br /> I want a Second Inquisition book.<br /> <br /> I want an Elders book.<br /> <br /> Oh and if I could order any, I'd want a Chronicle book for THE FALL OF VIENNA.</div> </div> </div> </div>I defo want Fall of Vienna so I can get my ST to run it for my Tremere character Charity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T05:55:02-08:00","id":1422415,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:8px\">(grumbling about no one commenting on my Python joke)</span><br /> <br /> We know we are getting more information (eventually) on cults, books on notable vampires, the Sabbat, the SI and a Player's Guide. In addition to that I want;<ul><li>I hope information on at least some of the blodlines - Salubri, Baali, Kiaysd, DoC - get detailed in the <i>Players Guide</i>, but I've heard that will not happen. So I hope they appear in some official (i.e. not a fan) book somewhere in the next few years.</li> <li>A chronicle book on the events in Vienna would be good.</li> <li>A new world tour book, like the <i>A World of Darkness</i> books from 1st and 2nd edition, would be nice. And it should have a lot of &quot;things&quot; that are not easily classified.</li> <li>Information on the drowned legacies.</li> <li>License out KotE and rework it utterly.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T08:11:11-08:00","id":1422426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1422413#post1422413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm eager for VtM V6<br /> <br /> or a fan edition like Pathfinder did for DnD<br /> <br /> they can nuke the sabat for all I care, I'm done waiting,<br /> I just hope they finally retcon all the dumb lore and start anew,<br /> and no more catering for LARP</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Metaplot can be salvaged. <br /> <br /> -The SI is the Camarilla solution. The &quot;Gehenna war&quot; is the Sabbat solution; the problem is too many fucking neonates. And so the Elders arranged for mass killings. <br /> -The beckoning is just elders hiding. <br /> -The Anarchs realise what a fucking bad idea they are (with some elder manipulation) and the Camarilla and Sabbat quickly swallow them up in their respective converging/reconquista. <br /> -The Hecata is a short lived idea that explodes to give us what we should've had for the past half milennium: Necromancers as an assortment of bloodlines that can be found in all sects. <br /> -The split of the Tremere is a rouse to deal with the fact that they are seen as villains, have far, far, far too many enemies and are a victim of their own monopolistic success. <br /> <br /> <br /> There are some things that can't be salvaged and need hard deletes (every mechanical change, the witches of echidna, thinblood changes) but it's certainly possible that the setting can come through these trying times without need for a nuke... I mean we haven't seen WTA yet. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T10:07:04-08:00","id":1422439,"title":"","content":"The fall of Vienna also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T10:48:37-08:00","id":1422447,"title":"","content":"In this case ,The Fall of Vienna is the centrepiece for the Tremere ploy to restructure and rebrand the pyramid. In which nobody loyal/important has died. <br /> The Tremere have long, long been a victim of their own success. The Tzmisce are reviled, the Lasombra are feared, and the Ravnos are vilified, but they don't do it quite on the scale of Tremere, who are the devil you have to deal with rather than the outsider you're free to despise. Tremere prestation is almost one-way, and they're far less smooth than the Setites when it comes to trading favours. <br /> The Tremere might be great. But the Tremere as a brand is terrible, and the moment they can be replaced, people will be dancing on the street. Providing an Illusion of choice and giving people the idea that they can deal with a Tremere without dealing with 'The Pyramid' is good. Going <i>down </i>to the laughably harmless witch-larp Tremere for a favour just doesn't seem as damning as going <i>up</i> to meet with <i>THE </i>Tremere. <br /> It also lets them put Tremere in cities that would never tolerate &quot;real&quot; Tremere. <br /> <br /> And as far as gameplay and immersion go, it's the only sensible choice to have all Tremere houses be loyal Tremere in truth. Otherwise, your city needs to pick a side and have only one kind of Tremere, because HT would stomp the naturally far smaller and weaker HC to keep their monopoly. If you have players that want to be with different Tremere houses (lord save you) these houses secretly being aligned is the only way to really do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T12:41:07-08:00","id":1422476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1422395#post1422395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A new edition of Dark Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This!<br /> <br /> Not that I have a problem with the existing DA - DA20 is my favorite rulebook - but I'd be very interested to see a DA rework using V5 rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T14:31:55-08:00","id":1422495,"title":"","content":"There's two main categories of books I'd like to see come from the new edition.<br /> <br /> 1. Faction/Lore Books: I'd love for more details on how Kindred organize around the world. Things like the Ashirra, Laibon, and even the Wan Kuei/Kuei-Jin all fascinate me. I know there's some controversy surrounding the game's past attempts at a broader cultural approach, but hopefully it can be done in a more respectful way this time around. I'd also love to see some stuff about the Second Inquisition and Sabbat, but I don't find myself as naturally drawn to them as I do the others.<br /> <br /> 2. Mechanics Books: I'm pretty much entirely new to the game and larger World of Darkness outside of a few glimpses at an old game story when I was in middle school. Trying to run my first chronicle has been challenging to say the least. The game doesn't really give new players or storytellers the tools they need to confidently tell a story unique to them and their experiences and the community as a whole doesn't really seem to have uniform advice or guidelines to help new consumers besides &quot;do what feels right&quot; which is...rather unhelpful when you have no previous exposure to the game or product line.<br /> <br /> A few books on running games in different time-frames would also be really nice, but those two categories should take priority in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25976-differentjustin","name":"DifferentJustin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T14:46:52-08:00","id":1422498,"title":"","content":"A book about the first or second city. I would even settle for carthage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T20:30:00-08:00","id":1422535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1422498#post1422498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A book about the first or second city. I would even settle for carthage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's someone working on a title for Storyteller's Vault along the lines of an Enoch by Night","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T01:33:47-08:00","id":1422568,"title":"","content":"DAV20 is the best and worst of the V20 line. It's got some great stuff (Celerity rework, Diamonion rework) some abhorent work (Quietus rework, witches of echidna) and some powers that exemplify what a mixed bag it is (Serpentis got rid of it's rituals but got extreme OPnss, Abyss mysticism is cool and I love that it's in a mainline book but it's broken as all hell, The Ahrimanes that kinda work for what they are but are written like a parody) and some well made art that says the wrong things...<br /> <br /> DAV20 isn't so much an aniversary as a reimagining, and I think it was set a hundred years after the last DA game which...<br /> <br /> I'd like a more 'proper' update to a DA book, really. The Better changes in DAV20 were for the most part, the more conservative ones, in my opinion at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T10:33:01-08:00","id":1422619,"title":"","content":"I would like something like Ghouls: Between Kine and Kindred, with extended rules for ghouls, ghoul animals/plants/etc. as well as hints about the remaining Revenants (some had to flood to the Camarilla once the Sabbat left) and the dhampyri, who got very little updating in V20. Also, combining a few of the previous ideas, Deviations of the Blood. Basically, a world tour featuring the main branches of the Kindred, like so:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Bloodlines: Kindred of the Shattered City- a brief update on a few of the major bloodlines, three to six, and how they came about/deal with the modern nights</li> <li>Ashirra: Kindred of the Scarlet Crescent- a take on how one of the oldest sects is different from the Camarilla</li> <li>Laibon: Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom- some say they are far descendants of Caine; others say they aren't Kindred at all; they themselves say both are true</li> <li>Drowned: Kindred of the New World- before Coumbus, they were here, but how and why</li> <li>Daeva: Kindred of the Midnight Castes (working title)- after the Week of Nightmares, India's Kindred have faced new challenges, and new opportunities</li> <li>Cathayans: Kindred of the Mysterious East- rumors abound of the Kindred from east Asia, but there isn't any truth to them, or is there?</li> </ol>It would be a catch-all book, with possible add-ons for more detailed supplements either as part of the original goal or future books. It's kind of a strange idea, but it could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T15:17:01-08:00","id":1423121,"title":"","content":"The Players guide would be fine. I would like also a book of Damascus by night, focusing on the Ashirra, Salubri and the Gehenna War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T16:48:10-08:00","id":1423140,"title":"","content":"Once the core rulebooks of the new editions of each of the primary game lines is out, I'd really like an authoritative guide to crossover campaigns. Game mechanics, storytelling tips, and food-for-thought details on how the material needs of each splat can complicate the existences of their allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T05:56:33-08:00","id":1423246,"title":"","content":"<b>Vampire: the Masquerade. 30th Aniversary edition</b>.<br /> <br /> A V5 edition with a good timeline of important things, extended information about the clans. With more power variations, rituals and background.<br /> Less like V20 where they added hundreds of bloodlines just to fill out the pages and less v20 disciplines that are OP.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>V5 Fall of the Sabbat</b><br /> Where we learn about the reasons and history of the Sabbat and how it crumbles as they went on their crusades. A book that gives to enough lore not to need any other book of previous versions of Vampire. Also about the Lasombra and Church of Caine leaving as well as the groups that remained and the loss of Mechikko City.<br /> <br /> <b>V5 Players Guide</b><br /> As told by Modiphius with added rules for Elders<br /> <br /> <b>V5 Fall of Vienna and the Scism of the Banu Haquim</b><br /> How the Tremere HQ fell and the way Banu Haquim and the Setites approached the Camarilla. Like small campaigns. Maybe the Return of the Salubri as the 13th clan.<br /> <br /> <b>V5 Second Inquisition</b><br /> As told by Modiphius<br /> <br /> <b>V5 Ashira Sect Book</b><br /> All information of the Sect<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T08:43:25-08:00","id":1423284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1423246#post1423246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Vampire: the Masquerade. 30th Aniversary edition</b>.<br /> <br /> A V5 edition with a good timeline of important things, extended information about the clans. With more power variations, rituals and background.<br /> Less like V20 where they added hundreds of bloodlines just to fill out the pages and less v20 disciplines that are OP.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>V5 Fall of the Sabbat</b><br /> Where we learn about the reasons and history of the Sabbat and how it crumbles as they went on their crusades. A book that gives to enough lore not to need any other book of previous versions of Vampire. Also about the Lasombra and Church of Caine leaving as well as the groups that remained and the loss of Mechikko City.<br /> <br /> <b>V5 Players Guide</b><br /> As told by Modiphius with added rules for Elders<br /> <br /> <b>V5 Fall of Vienna and the Scism of the Banu Haquim</b><br /> How the Tremere HQ fell and the way Banu Haquim and the Setites approached the Camarilla. Like small campaigns. Maybe the Return of the Salubri as the 13th clan.<br /> <br /> <b>V5 Second Inquisition</b><br /> As told by Modiphius<br /> <br /> <b>V5 Ashira Sect Book</b><br /> All information of the Sect</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is this satirical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T09:14:16-08:00","id":1423291,"title":"","content":"We need a book for mechanics and storylines centering around playing Elders and Methuselahs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T12:51:11-08:00","id":1423624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1423284#post1423284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is this satirical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, that is what I want. I like v5, and i Think V20 was more for munchkins who want to play OP vampires. I seriously dislike the idea of bloodpoints as it is a tracker that you have control over and i favour the random hunger that is in the V5.<br /> <br /> Also I like the new potence, celerity and fortitude over the old versions and although i dislike the merging of disciplines. It is a minor fault of the system. The disciplines are uch less Op than in V20 which is good in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T17:23:05-08:00","id":1423653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1423246#post1423246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As told by Modiphius<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well......thats not gonna happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T20:47:41-08:00","id":1425087,"title":"","content":"I would want a bunch of Metaplot chronicles like Fall of London<br /> <br /> 1) Fall of Vienna: A tremere only chronicle in Vienna that dealt with the House Carna and the Second Inquisition. It could have multiple possible endings involving the survival of some of the members of the council or their entire downfall<br /> <br /> 2) A theo bell/ Hardestadt council: An elder campaign where players play power politics at the fateful meeting where allegedly Theo Bell turned traitor. What cause it? What were they issues? Is Theo really a double agent?<br /> <br /> 3) A sabbat crusade and Lasombra chronicle: A sabbat pack on crusade in the middle East would discover the secret of Lasombra's survival and then have to escape as Lasombra sent minions to try and stop them. A sort of military and survival story against steep odds.<br /> <br /> 4) A setite/assamite meeting chronicle: Players might be the investigators following up on that fated meeting where the setites were killed. They would have to unravel the true source of the attacks.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T22:12:43-08:00","id":1425091,"title":"","content":"VDA5 would be splendid, although I feel like a lot of the changes in V5 are meant to be post-Withering so it would be interesting to see where it'd go.<br /> <br /> Right now the one thing I really want is already in the Companion, and that's just material on coteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T01:22:08-08:00","id":1425108,"title":"","content":"Tokyo by Night - the section in the Camarilla book on it sounded fascinating and I would love to see this book some day<br /> <br /> Ashirra sect guide - Something a bit different, I want to see how it differs from the Camarilla and also it's a good way of making V5 feel more global<br /> <br /> V5 Ancient Rome: A chronicle and setting guide for playing in the Ancient Roman era - Dark Ages would be cool as well but I think Rome is such an interesting period for Vampires and I'd love to have more lore on that and advice for playing around that time.<br /> <br /> Second Inquisition book: We've heard this may be coming in the future anyway, I think it's a great idea and I'm looking forward to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26541-kninj","name":"kninj","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T01:48:37-08:00","id":1425110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425091#post1425091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VDA5 would be splendid, although I feel like a lot of the changes in V5 are meant to be post-Withering so it would be interesting to see where it'd go.<br /> <br /> Right now the one thing I really want is already in the Companion, and that's just material on coteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this &quot;Withering&quot; thing an actual canon thing or is it something made up by the fanbase to explain V5's shift in mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T03:02:27-08:00","id":1425118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425110#post1425110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this &amp;quot;Withering&amp;quot; thing an actual canon thing or is it something made up by the fanbase to explain V5's shift in mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its from one of the Gehenna book scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T03:38:56-08:00","id":1425123,"title":"","content":"After the V5 Sabbat book I mostly wish for a V5 Ashirra book. Or at least a Damascus/Bagdad by Night one. And I really hope that the arabic clan versions get new symbols and not the gibberish pseudo-arabic ones they had before. Something along the lines of the new Banu Hakim clan symbol would be nice. Or something calligraphic.<br /> <br /> Also an extra ' Advanced/optional rules companion' with something like 'rule modules' would be nice. Like the advanced combat rules in the core book but for other aspects of the game. Rules for elders, rules for more than five powers per discpline while at the same time keeping the 'maximum 5 dots'-rule, alternative diablerie rules that follow the rules of the memoriam, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T04:15:35-08:00","id":1425134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kninj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425108#post1425108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Inquisition book: We've heard this may be coming in the future anyway, I think it's a great idea and I'm looking forward to it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Though hopefully less Blade knock offs than the ones in Fall of London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T08:43:32-08:00","id":1425169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425110#post1425110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this &quot;Withering&quot; thing an actual canon thing or is it something made up by the fanbase to explain V5's shift in mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was a plot thing in the Gehenna book, which was ignored by V5's timeline advancement. A lot of people talk about it as a thing, but it's not actually in V5 at all. People just use it for self-justification of why the scale is different, rather than just accepting that the overall scale of V5's power levels are different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T09:00:12-08:00","id":1425172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425169#post1425169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It was a plot thing in the Gehenna book, which was ignored by V5's timeline advancement. A lot of people talk about it as a thing, but it's not actually in V5 at all. People just use it for self-justification of why the scale is different, rather than just accepting that the overall scale of V5's power levels are different.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Different he mean way lower btw)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T09:09:24-08:00","id":1425175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425172#post1425172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Different he mean way lower btw)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's representative of the entire scale being DIFFERENT than what it was in prior ediitons. People ignore the scale across the board is different, lower overall; it's not meant to have the same 'Joe Neonate has seventeen things at five after six months of play because XP glut and gaming the front-end of the system' power scale that prior editions did.<br /> <br /> But way to low-key edition war, bud!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T14:36:46-08:00","id":1425243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425169#post1425169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It was a plot thing in the Gehenna book, which was ignored by V5's timeline advancement. A lot of people talk about it as a thing, but it's not actually in V5 at all. People just use it for self-justification of why the scale is different, rather than just accepting that the overall scale of V5's power levels are different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to me referring to it as a possible explanation <i>is</i> acceptance.<br /> <br /> Then you have people who don't like that you can't do the really powerful methuselah stuff in V5, yet V5 uses the same continuity ... because V5 has no in-book explanation. This has nothing to do with how fast PCs advanced in previous editions, but rather with established setting events such as Menele causing a volcanic eruption with blood magic, or another methuselah using presence to manipulate an entire city.<br /> <br /> For the record, I believe Martin Ericsson referred to the withering and the beckoning both as the cause of the setting's overall depowering, and V5 was explicitly presented as post-Gehenna, just a different scenario from those in the book. It didn't reach its logical conclusion and didn't work the same way, but it's a thing I believe was said early on. I'd look for it in the video from the grand masquerade in 2017 or 2018 (I think) but I don't want to watch any more of that guy than I absolutely have to.<br /> <br /> I don't mind the lower power level or lack of Disciplines at 6+. That's fine.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my original statement was that I personally feel like the withering explains the changes, so it's not something anyone else needs. I just object to the notion that finding or having an explanation for the transition is somehow a <i>lack of acceptance</i>. My refusal to touch V5 until this month was a lack of acceptance. This is me accepting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-20-2020, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T17:35:11-08:00","id":1425277,"title":"","content":"Gehenna War. with perspectives from all sides of the conflict.<br /> Infernalism - from the common and boringly spooky Nergali to 'Radical Inquisition' Molochim to some regional and crossover phenomena like possessed or cursed vampires; new, enigmatic bloodlines mistakenly identified as a Baali offshot, etc.<br /> Anything Paths (like Chaining the Beast)<br /> Vampire warfare/espionage books, like Midnight Siege, one of my favorite ones from the Revised.<br /> Second Inquisition would be great.<br /> \u200bAnything Sabbat.<br /> Anything metaplot heavy - Tal'Mahe'Ra, Inconnu you name it.<br /> Vampire Nomads! not just Sabbat but any vamps who chose the unlife on the road<br /> Regional supplements and sourcebooks for games set in South America, MENA, India, Central Asia and Eastern Europe. I would gladly help with one.<br /> Cities by Night are ALWAYS welcome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T18:40:50-08:00","id":1425292,"title":"","content":"A city making guide similar to Requiem's Damnation City?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T19:37:30-08:00","id":1425300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425292#post1425292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A city making guide similar to Requiem's Damnation City?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be all for something like this. As much as I love the backstory and the setting, I really want more information and guidance on the mechanics from a Storyteller\u2019s point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25976-differentjustin","name":"DifferentJustin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T20:16:53-08:00","id":1425307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kninj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425108#post1425108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 Ancient Rome: A chronicle and setting guide for playing in the Ancient Roman era - Dark Ages would be cool as well but I think Rome is such an interesting period for Vampires and I'd love to have more lore on that and advice for playing around that time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see something like this, if for no other reason to see what the various European Clans considered their creations myth(s) to be in pre-Christian times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T21:19:10-08:00","id":1425311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425307#post1425307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see something like this, if for no other reason to see what the various European Clans considered their creations myth(s) to be in pre-Christian times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we had a thread talking about that earlier this year. I can't recall much of specifics about it though, other than that there was a pre-Republic snake goddess cult in central Italy that would make an interesting if odd potential Setite origin. <br /> <br /> Last time I did anything with Dark Ages, I had the generally accepted mythology be that the 13 founders were fallen angels, with the High Clan ones having fallen for &quot;noble&quot; reasons and the Low Clans for base ones. (I tend to ignore the 2nd gen altogether.) <br /> <br /> (In a more perfect world, I like to believe the three historical lines would've been Vampire the Dark Ages, Werewolf: Savage Rome, and Mage: Victorian Twilight, and each having books about the other groups during that time. Mage the Dark Ages, Savage Rome by Night, Victorian Werewolf, etc. But I am weird.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T21:51:09-08:00","id":1425316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425307#post1425307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see something like this, if for no other reason to see what the various European Clans considered their creations myth(s) to be in pre-Christian times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love something like that as well, but the more I think about it, the more problematic it gets. Best case scenario is they outline a bunch of options to deal with that and create branched characters for the various potential mythologies. Worst case they'd double down on just one canon preChristian origin. Do you shoe horn in the Caine story in a world where barely anybody outside the Levant had heard the story? Do you have another story, with possibly multiple origins for different clans, and if so what are they? Do you go with the Caine story's a myth or metaphor that gained traction later? Do you double down on the Caine story but make it so that only the very oldest vampires knew it was true and most vampires in the ancient era weren't aware of it? It's definitely a bit of a minefield with a lot of potential to screw it up. Anything but presenting a bunch of possibilities, ala Gehenna/Beckett's Jyhad Diary story hooks, seems like a bad idea. If they went with the idea of pick one of these many different scenarios for how things worked, it could be really cool, though, especially if they present NPCs in the lore with multiple options for if X is true or they believe it than they behave this way, but if Y is true or they believe it the NPC goes this way. Anything else is too much risk of pissing a lot of people off or getting things completely wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T23:17:44-08:00","id":1425320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425316#post1425316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything but presenting a bunch of possibilities, ala Gehenna/Beckett's Jyhad Diary story hooks, seems like a bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the era, it would almost have to be.<br /> <br /> Vampires are parasites, and their Roman hosts' beliefs were polytheistic and syncretic, more willing to absorb and merge foreign ideas with their own to preserve societal order than to stamp them out outright. You'd probably have vampiric scholars who believe their particular theories were the One True Way and willing to shed blood over it, but you'd have just as many trying to fit other beliefs into their own model, or use competing ideas to explain the Clans' different strengths and weaknesses. Ancients would have beliefs placing their origin anywhere from Utnapishtim to Angra Mainyu to the <i>striges</i> to Pluto and Orpheus, and you'd have vampires debating, arguing, synthesizing, and/or ignoring all of the above, and it'd be <i><b>great</b></i>.<br /> <br /> ...though, given that VtM seems fixated on the Cain[e] mythos being the actual One True Way, it's probably for the best that book isn't a thing, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T16:49:09-08:00","id":1425407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425307#post1425307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see something like this, if for no other reason to see what the various European Clans considered their creations myth(s) to be in pre-Christian times.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a book that was released like today on Storytellers Vault that I believe covers this time period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T17:03:37-08:00","id":1425408,"title":"","content":"I'd love a Chronicle book set around LA by Night, Seattle, and maybe Austin or Tuscon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T09:37:36-08:00","id":1425531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425408#post1425408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love a Chronicle book set around LA by Night, Seattle, and maybe Austin or Tuscon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's the Live Plays in LA and Seatle, and games based out of Tuscon and Seattle. I don't know if that is more likely or less likely to result in a chronicle book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T17:49:34-08:00","id":1425593,"title":"","content":"A Seattle by Night would be cool but not sure if needed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T18:08:46-08:00","id":1425595,"title":"","content":"How should a city with an ongoing chronicle (L.A. by Night, Seattle by Night, any of the other official ones) be handled? The nature of the ongoing chronicle, with its PCs, can make it feel rather insular as compared to something like Chicago by Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T18:39:51-08:00","id":1425600,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think any sourcebook should chain itself to an ongoing chronicle. If you did books for Seattle or LA, you could reference the chronicles, but needing or even just expecting people to stay up to date with them is excessive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T19:35:18-08:00","id":1425610,"title":"","content":"Wait do those big on-youtube games become canonical? That'd be moronic, and even if you could get the greatest table to do em it would still kinda suck because you'd be denying players cities in a way. ( Players like to think their games are just as legit as other games)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T19:39:42-08:00","id":1425613,"title":"","content":"Wasn't some weird board game that was going to be played by some big-shots were going to be canon in the series before? Not like the Tabletop itself, but just literally some boardgame. I forgot which thread in this site brought it up, but its hilarious that such sessions after they're played become CANON for whatever inane reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-23-2020, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T19:53:44-08:00","id":1425616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want#post1422370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Know, or at least expected books, for the V5 line include; Cults of the Blood Gods, the Player's Handbook, Forbidden Faiths, Olsen's Standard Book of British Birds, Children of the Blood and probably Sabbat.<br /> <br /> But what books do you want to see released? What subject matters do you want covered?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred of the East<br /> <br /> Legacies of the Drowned.<br /> <br /> Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom<br /> <br /> City Book for a South American City like Rio and City Book for something Like Singapore or New Deli. But make these after they are ready to cover the area rather then ignore the weird aspects of the area that need to be covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T20:09:28-08:00","id":1425619,"title":"","content":"What I would really like, would be:<br /> <br /> #1: Ancient Blood: The Book of Elders (or, Book of The Beckoning - the Elders' Masquerade from the neonates),<br /> <br /> #2: The Sabbat (I'm really thinking that the Sabbat is imploding in the V5 timeline, and I really think that it would be epically entertaining),<br /> <br /> #3: Second Inquisition<br /> <br /> #4: A V5 version of Damnation City from VtR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","user":"Japheth","date":". 11-22-2020, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T21:53:13-08:00","id":1425645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425610#post1425610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait do those big on-youtube games become canonical? That'd be moronic, and even if you could get the greatest table to do em it would still kinda suck because you'd be denying players cities in a way. ( Players like to think their games are just as legit as other games)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Last I heard all the different product streams are canon, so the board games set canon NPCs etc. for the tabletop cities they are set in, Visual novels determine ( non player facing) events for background in the tabletop, not sure on the card games but I would assume at least the NPCs established would be likewise treated as canon.<br /> <br /> Officially sanctioned streaming games set canon for the tabletop as far as I'm aware.<br /> <br /> Yeah......its a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T21:55:10-08:00","id":1425646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425616#post1425616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred of the East<br /> <br /> Legacies of the Drowned.<br /> <br /> Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love them to do a serious rethink of how they approached vampires in Asia, South America, and Africa and provide something more in like with Masquerade, but without the Orientalism of KotE especially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T21:55:35-08:00","id":1425647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425616#post1425616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred of the East<br /> <br /> Legacies of the Drowned.<br /> <br /> Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom<br /> <br /> City Book for a South American City like Rio and City Book for something Like Singapore or New Deli. But make these after they are ready to cover the area rather then ignore the weird aspects of the area that need to be covered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be very surprised if they ever touch the first three. And if they did they'd probably just make everyone viral-vamps and squish them into the existing Clans.<br /> <br /> Theres some pretty good versions of the fourth one on the Vault written by locals, I'd wager that you won't get anything canon for a very long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T22:27:00-08:00","id":1425660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425647#post1425647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd be very surprised if they ever touch the first three. And if they did they'd probably just make everyone viral-vamps and squish them into the existing Clans.<br /> <br /> Theres some pretty good versions of the fourth one on the Vault written by locals, I'd wager that you won't get anything canon for a very long time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way it looks like its going to go, they're working on the major plotline. I just don't think there are enough fans of KotE and the Laibon to justify a large splatbook for them. Of course, this is only my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T23:01:55-08:00","id":1425663,"title":"","content":"I mean you don't need fans you make new fans with new products otherwise new anything doesn't work.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425647#post1425647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd be very surprised if they ever touch the first three. And if they did they'd probably just make everyone viral-vamps and squish them into the existing Clans.<br /> <br /> Theres some pretty good versions of the fourth one on the Vault written by locals, I'd wager that you won't get anything canon for a very long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vault is probably the only way I would get anything I would actually like I feel it may end up being more satisfying then a mainstream book made to be safe. A Rio book made by a Local you say? Hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T23:54:55-08:00","id":1425667,"title":"","content":"To be honest, if we are getting the Vampire Companion now, I don\u2019t really feel the need for a Players Guide.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d welcome The Sabbat book, if it is done in the same way as the Camarilla and Anarchs books, and possibly incorporating/duplicating the Tzmisce and Lasombra from other sourcebooks. heck, maybe even incorporating the Ravnos. I\u2019d like to see The Second Inquisition as almost a spin-off game. I\u2019d like to see more City and Chronicle books spanning the globe. If it is going to take a while to get to any form of Wraith new edition, if ever, then I\u2019d like to see supplements that integrate ghosts and spirits into the new game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T02:55:04-08:00","id":1425689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, if we are getting the Vampire Companion now, I don\u2019t really feel the need for a Players Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a Companion book and a Players Guide are basically the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T06:15:39-08:00","id":1425716,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a book of bloodlines with fresh playable options.<br /> <br /> I'm not interested in another glut of city by night books. I think with Chicago by Night as good as it is, any Storyteller should be able to refer to that and build their own city instead of holding out for a city book to define other domains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T10:28:16-08:00","id":1425760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425689#post1425689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So a Companion book and a Players Guide are basically the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>For my purposes, essentially they are. I wouldn\u2019t feel the need to get both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T10:54:31-08:00","id":1425761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425760#post1425760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For my purposes, essentially they are. I wouldn\u2019t feel the need to get both.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they promised that in PG we will get more playstyles!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T11:20:16-08:00","id":1425765,"title":"","content":"I'm still thinking that The Beckoning is the Elders' Masquerade against their childer, and we need an Elders sourcebook, much like what <i>War of Ages</i> did for <i>VtM 2nd Edition</i> onward.<br /> <br /> Maybe have them (Elders) have extra dice to wield when they have Blood Potency over a certain threshold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","user":"Japheth","date":". 11-23-2020, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T11:25:12-08:00","id":1425767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stannis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425716#post1425716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see a book of bloodlines with fresh playable options.<br /> <br /> I'm not interested in another glut of city by night books. I think with Chicago by Night as good as it is, any Storyteller should be able to refer to that and build their own city instead of holding out for a city book to define other domains.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtR had a sensational book, entitled <i>Damnation City</i> that delved into the sandbox/crunch of city building. An updated one for V5 would really be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T18:36:56-08:00","id":1425824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425761#post1425761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they promised that in PG we will get more playstyles!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m happy with the playstyles presented in the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T20:08:45-08:00","id":1425840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Japheth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425765#post1425765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still thinking that The Beckoning is the Elders' Masquerade against their childer, and we need an Elders sourcebook, much like what <i>War of Ages</i> did for <i>VtM 2nd Edition</i> onward.<br /> <br /> Maybe have them (Elders) have extra dice to wield when they have Blood Potency over a certain threshold.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would be the point of having an Elder book when the entire settings mechanic dynamic has been capsized to be weaker and Disciplines are only stuck at a flat 5 dots, which is merely Anchillae tier? I doubt they will ever do any Elder material with the current design philosophy surrounding V5, they want to keep things relegated to a weak street or neonate-tier style of play only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T20:31:42-08:00","id":1425843,"title":"","content":"What was the point of having an elder book for V:tR in that case?<br /> <br /> It's worth it, and it can explore the elder-ness in a cool way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T07:55:21-08:00","id":1425956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425843#post1425843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the point of having an elder book for V:tR in that case?<br /> <br /> It's worth it, and it can explore the elder-ness in a cool way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree.<br /> <br /> To dovetail with my point about an Elders book, playing neonates are fun and all; the lack of elder vampire creation seems to be a huge oversight for those of us whom have been playing VtM more than twenty years.<br /> <br /> Let's face it, playing an elder vampire brings into a whole new element --- POWER!!! Elders have the power, and neonates don't. If anything, an Elders book would allow Storytellers the tools to create a truly monstrous kindred of elder power, be it the Prince of a city, Justicars and their archons, and if its true that there's a Sabbat book in 2021/2022, then you'll be able to see Templars, Cardinals, and so on up the power ladder.<br /> <br /> Also, if there's ever a V5 DAV, we will need to have the means to create an elder vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","user":"Japheth","date":". 11-24-2020, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:11:28-08:00","id":1425988,"title":"","content":"Do you really need an elder book? The rules have already made things very clear: <br /> There are no 6+ disciplines. <br /> Blood potency 5+ is... extraordinarily difficult to play given hunger mechanics. But it's all written down if you want it. <br /> <br /> Just add XP. All the mechanics are there for you in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T10:18:18-08:00","id":1425992,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat book easily tops the list for me. If it's designed the way I hope it is, it will focus heavily on activities in the middle east and be much more combative and less political. Something for players who want to run head long into the fray rather than play long social and political games.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see a book to present alternative optional rules to change aspects of the system for GMs that want to cater their game to their vision. I'm guessing this would be the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> Clan books would be really nice too, although I'd prefer to see larger themed books covering multiple clans instead of twelve or thirteen small ones.<br /> <br /> Some more city books would be nice. I would LOVE a new Montreal By Night (being someone who lives there) showing the recent history there and how the factions in that city have changes. I'd also prefer it if there were still some Sabbat in the city. The wonderful thing about the Montreal Sabbat is they were much more spiritual than combative. More focused on their Path philosophies and their approach to morality and dealing with humans. I don't want to lose that and I'm hoping many of the more religious and philosophical Sabbat are still present and have come to an uneasy truce with both the Camarilla and Anarchs to create a triple faction city. Sort of like a kindred Jerusalem where there is peace, but barely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T17:41:15-08:00","id":1426058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425988#post1425988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you really need an elder book? The rules have already made things very clear:<br /> There are no 6+ disciplines.<br /> Blood potency 5+ is... extraordinarily difficult to play given hunger mechanics. But it's all written down if you want it.<br /> <br /> Just add XP. All the mechanics are there for you in the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>The V:tR elder book as well as Elysium provided far more than &quot;more dots for everyone.&quot; I referenced Thousand Years of Night specifically because V:tR also has a five dot limit on disciplines. I specifically mean the non-mechanical stuff.<br /> <br /> For example, one topic that could use coverage is how elders tend to prefer feeding. But also, I think you're overstating the difficulty elders have with feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T03:42:30-08:00","id":1426102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426058#post1426058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I specifically mean the non-mechanical stuff<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>...more in-character, unreliable narrator babble in italic? Like cam and anarch books?<br /> <br /> e_e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T04:01:42-08:00","id":1426105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426102#post1426102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...more in-character, unreliable narrator babble in italic? Like cam and anarch books?<br /> <br /> e_e</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I mean discussion about what elders are like.<br /> <br /> In the unlikely event that such a book came to pass, it'd have the italic parts no matter what so why worry?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T04:38:39-08:00","id":1426113,"title":"","content":"Given how 2020 has turned out, I wouldn't actually mind a &quot;timeline/metaplot update book&quot;. I don't think any real-world event since World War II will have had this much effect on the unlife and world of Vampire, so a book on how the Pandemic changed things could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Also, a new edition of Dark Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T14:09:48-08:00","id":1426176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426113#post1426113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how 2020 has turned out, I wouldn't actually mind a &quot;timeline/metaplot update book&quot;. I don't think any real-world event since World War II will have had this much effect on the unlife and world of Vampire, so a book on how the Pandemic changed things could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Also, a new edition of Dark Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Achilli spoke a little about this on a recent podcast. He seemed open to the idea of 2020 metaplot updates but understandably cautious about doing them while people are still bearing the brunt.<br /> <br /> I <i>absolutely </i>agree about a new Dark Ages, though<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T14:48:48-08:00","id":1426179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1425840#post1425840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would be the point of having an Elder book when the entire settings mechanic dynamic has been capsized to be weaker and Disciplines are only stuck at a flat 5 dots, which is merely Anchillae tier? I doubt they will ever do any Elder material with the current design philosophy surrounding V5, they want to keep things relegated to a weak street or neonate-tier style of play only.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take a different view. I like elders because they're <i>old</i>. They've seen a lot of history. They've lived through the Transylvania Chronicles or the Giovanni Chronicles or the Ventrue Chronicles or whatever. They're a rich source of the lore and backstory which is Masquerade's great strength and makes books like BJD possible<br /> <br /> What I did <i>not </i>like about them in the earlier editions was that they were peers of the Great bloody Cthulhu. I'd rather have them as old, powerful vampires than demigods. I'm aware that others feel differently and like the elders-as-demigods aspect as part and parcel of the setting - chacun \u00e0 son go\u00fbt. But I don't personally see the lack of attributes at 6+ as destroying the point of an elder book. It might, for instance, consider Touchstones, elder coteries, questions of memory (some rules for how easily an elder remembers an event five hundred or a thousand years ago without resorting to Memoriam would be useful).<br /> <br /> It might also challenge a few too-entrenched stereotypes. (Off the top of my head, remember the scene in LA by Night when Hester uses a bowl of water to communicate with Strauss? We can probably assume that Strauss has been doing &quot;video conferencing&quot; since the middle ages. He's unlikely to struggle conceptually with facetime on an iPhone, as the &quot;elders as anachronisms&quot; schtick assumes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T18:04:50-08:00","id":1426403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426176#post1426176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>absolutely </i>agree about a new Dark Ages, though</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, why? Why not simply use V5 rules in a VDA setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T00:46:10-08:00","id":1426431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426403#post1426403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, why? Why not simply use V5 rules in a VDA setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they made a 20th Anniversary Edition of Dark Ages after V20... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, there a number of things you'd need for a Dark Ages book that V5 doesn't have (yet), like all the Clans, at least a couple of Bloodlines, non-merged Disciplines, a different, more expansive section on weapons and armor. As well as how the clans looked in the Middle Ages. By then, you might as well just add some historical information and make it its own book.<br /> <br /> Also, I absolutely love Dark Ages, so a new edition would be great.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T04:10:49-08:00","id":1426445,"title":"","content":"&quot;Non-merged disciplines&quot; <br /> Whut, who are you? Royalty? The Changes to vampires in V5 isn't part of some withering, they're a hard retcon; Those disciplines were <i>always </i>merged, and the V5 weapon/armour table is inclusive of all possible options. Once we have all the clans, V5 rules cover everything except infernalism. all you want for a dark ages game is maybe some vampire alt-historical information and maybe a bloodline or two (But you can invent bloodlines pretty easily)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T09:24:38-08:00","id":1426471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426445#post1426445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Non-merged disciplines&quot;<br /> Whut, who are you? Royalty? The Changes to vampires in V5 isn't part of some withering, they're a hard retcon</div> </div> </div> </div>The absence of discipline paths complicates necromancy in particular, for games set before the Family Reunion. Samedi, Giovanni, Nagaraja etc. can also use the same powers and ceremonies because as Hecata (by default), they're all comparring notes. Whereas even a generation ago, very few of them were. So what did Cappadocians and Giovanni Cappadocians know before they met Samedi, Pisanob, Mla Watu and Nagaraja, before the Harbingers spent a few centuries in the underworld and when the Giovanni were still fairly new to being kindred?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T10:11:32-08:00","id":1426478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426445#post1426445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Non-merged disciplines&quot;<br /> Whut, who are you? Royalty? The Changes to vampires in V5 isn't part of some withering, they're a hard retcon; Those disciplines were <i>always </i>merged, and the V5 weapon/armour table is inclusive of all possible options. Once we have all the clans, V5 rules cover everything except infernalism. all you want for a dark ages game is maybe some vampire alt-historical information and maybe a bloodline or two (But you can invent bloodlines pretty easily)</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not 100% up on it, but if I understood correctly, Oblivion is a merger of Obtenebration and Necromancy, which begs the questions why the Cappadocians Embraced the Giovanni if their powers were already around.<br /> <br /> Also, the weapons and armor table at the very least needs ruled for shields. But also for the types of armor that were around in the Middle Ages. And I would personally like a bit more gradiation so there is a diffference between an arming sword, a battle axe and a mace, though I am probably a minority here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T11:37:40-08:00","id":1426483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426478#post1426478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not 100% up on it, but if I understood correctly, Oblivion is a merger of Obtenebration and Necromancy, which begs the questions why the Cappadocians Embraced the Giovanni if their powers were already around.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they did it for the Rituals, or maybe they needed the Giovanni's influence over mortals, including their wealth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T12:50:42-08:00","id":1426486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426403#post1426403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, why? Why not simply use V5 rules in a VDA setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, but it would be interesting to see if they could combine the medieval Roads with the new morality system, there would be different skills on the character sheet, you could have an update on developments in Cainite society... plenty of scope for a book, or at least a V5 medieval companion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T14:29:19-08:00","id":1426496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426483#post1426483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they did it for the Rituals, or maybe they needed the Giovanni's influence over mortals, including their wealth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the story so far has always been that they did it for the Giovanni family\u2019s Necromancy, which allowed a different and unique insight ito death, specifically dealing with Wraith and the Underworld/Shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T14:47:56-08:00","id":1426500,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the Cappadocians were originally more geared towards the physical side of necromancy while the Giovanni understood the spiritual side of necromancy better than they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T00:28:00-08:00","id":1426542,"title":"","content":"v5 could explain it with rituals? <br /> personally, i think the physical Mortis practices are second rate compared to the necromancy paths like sephulcre and ash, to the point where i wonder why the capadocians never realized it and didn't switch long ago. Having there be little/no difference on the main path may be a good way to equalize things. <br /> /devils advocate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T04:04:12-08:00","id":1426558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426500#post1426500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, the Cappadocians were originally more geared towards the physical side of necromancy while the Giovanni understood the spiritual side of necromancy better than they did.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep. For a V5 Dark Ages book to make sense, they'd have to establish a clear difference in Necromantic schools (i.e Paths), which is something V5 clearly has abandoned as a game philosophy (that is no shoehorned &quot;&quot;streamlines&quot;&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T06:03:29-08:00","id":1426571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426542#post1426542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">v5 could explain it with rituals?<br /> personally, i think the physical Mortis practices are second rate compared to the necromancy paths like sephulcre and ash, to the point where i wonder why the capadocians never realized it and didn't switch long ago. Having there be little/no difference on the main path may be a good way to equalize things.<br /> /devils advocate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't they embrace the Giovanni precisely because they needed them to develop spiritual necromancy as an application of Mortis? And hence Giovanni don't bother with most physical aspects of Mortis anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T06:19:38-08:00","id":1426573,"title":"","content":"I think that's half true, they embraced the Giovanni in part because they were impressed by their ability to use necromancy for ghosts, but contacting ghosts wouldn't have been a Giovanni-exclusive at the time, There are much more people around the globe who would claim to contact ghosts than there are people who would claim powers of messing with corpse-properties after all. I doubt the Capadocians <i>needed </i>the giovanni, they just wanted the giovanni. <br /> I can't remember the date cited for when the Flesh eaters were embraced, I think they're pretty ancient, but they were using the spiritual paths long ago and they don't have much to do with the main clan. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T06:27:14-08:00","id":1426576,"title":"","content":"The Nagaraja weren't embraced, they like the Tremere, used a ritual to turn themselves into Vampires with Vitae as the ingredient. It was Setite blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T06:32:52-08:00","id":1426577,"title":"","content":"Yeah but when? I think it's ancient, but for all i know it could've been two hundred years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T06:40:47-08:00","id":1426578,"title":"","content":"All we know was that they obtained the sample right around the time the 2nd City (Enoch) was about to collapse from the growing instability. So that's a really long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T09:31:50-08:00","id":1426596,"title":"","content":"I would like books that are published on time. Bonus points if they have been properly edited and are not full of plot holes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T13:09:13-08:00","id":1426614,"title":"","content":"As a wishlist?<br /> <br /> Elder Book - Fix the mechanics. Bring the scope of the original game back. Stop making VtM into VtR. Both are great games. Their settings define them. They're different.<br /> <br /> Sabbat Book - The Sabbat declares victory after getting their teeth kicked in for two decades and has to limp back to Europe and NA as a secret elite society of war veterans. Fix the Humanity mechanics. <br /> <br /> Banu Haqim and Lasombra Books - Clan civil wars sound really cool.<br /> <br /> Blood Sorcery Book - Fix the mechanics. <br /> <br /> Anarch and Camarilla Books - But this time, less gay genocide and make it an Actual Useful Book. How do vampires siege cities under the eye of the SI? <br /> <br /> Baali Book - Reveal that Rudi is Tanithbaal-Sahar and that they are taking advantage of the diminished stability to Raise the Children.<br /> <br /> Second Inquisition - Reveal it's the Technocracy considering Vampires a credible threat to Consensus after The Bangladesh Incident of 1999. Secret Vatican drone strikes and cabals of government agents tie in perfectly to the good old Order of Reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gogo Baccala<br /> <br /> Drag Queen, Ex-Attorney, Freelance Deity","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26376-gogobaccala","name":"Gogobaccala","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T16:56:06-08:00","id":1426637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426445#post1426445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Non-merged disciplines&quot;<br /> Whut, who are you? Royalty? The Changes to vampires in V5 isn't part of some withering, they're a hard retcon; Those disciplines were <i>always </i>merged, and the V5 weapon/armour table is inclusive of all possible options. Once we have all the clans, V5 rules cover everything except infernalism. all you want for a dark ages game is maybe some vampire alt-historical information and maybe a bloodline or two (But you can invent bloodlines pretty easily)</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not a retcon in any game I run. Should I ever run V5.<br /> <br /> If they do a Vampire: The Dark Ages 5 and make it clear it's a retcon, that's fine. I'll ignore the rules and use VtDA20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-29-2020, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T03:20:18-08:00","id":1426674,"title":"","content":"would it be nice to have a book on the infernal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T18:08:16-08:00","id":1426775,"title":"","content":"Infernalism is always a favorite, a bit of pure black to contrast against the shades of gray. Would also be cool to update the Baali in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T15:19:26-08:00","id":1427495,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a book that extensively details mortal Blood Bound thralls, and mortals under the sway of Presence and Dominate powers. I even have a nice name for it: <i>the Bound and the Beholden</i>. I feel that this very expansive aspect of Vampires' control over mortals and their societies and institutions has not been given the treatment that it should have. Over half of the 13 Clans have either Presence or Dominate (and the Ventrue have both). There's a lot to write about. There is a tremendous variety in types of servants that a Vampire might have. It has to be noted that within Presence and Dominate, each Power influences differently. Blood Bonding mortals without ghouling is an area that has a lot of potential to explore. Then there are Clan specific approaches to methods of influence and control to be considered.<br /> As a plus, such a book could also cover animal servants (both Animalism related, and Ghouls), mortal lovers (and treasured mortal friends) of Vampires, and the few mortal families which exist under the purview of Vampires.<br /> <br /> Writing this got me thinking - Disciplines specific books might be another idea. Though currently, I think that only Presence and Dominate would provide enough of material and focus to be written about extensively enough for a book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-07-2020, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T20:00:55-08:00","id":1427515,"title":"","content":"There's ghoul stuff in the upcoming V5 Companion, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T11:03:16-08:00","id":1428286,"title":"","content":"More about Ghouls is all good, but I'd really would like to hear more about what exactly it does to a mortal when they are exposed to the Presence powers (especially Summon or multiple uses of Awe) ; or just how numerous mortal Thralls are. The Blood Bound businessman or stockbroker of a Ventrue Vampire is known, but there is definitely room to explore in regard to Blood Binding the less well-placed mortals who can be very useful. (Blood Bind a person in city transportation, and you can alter the bus routes, for example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-13-2020, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T02:58:17-08:00","id":1428839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gogobaccala</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1426614#post1426614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a wishlist?<br /> <br /> Elder Book - Fix the mechanics. Bring the scope of the original game back. Stop making VtM into VtR. Both are great games. Their settings define them. They're different.<br /> <br /> Sabbat Book - The Sabbat declares victory after getting their teeth kicked in for two decades and has to limp back to Europe and NA as a secret elite society of war veterans. Fix the Humanity mechanics. <br /> <br /> Banu Haqim and Lasombra Books - Clan civil wars sound really cool.<br /> <br /> Blood Sorcery Book - Fix the mechanics. <br /> <br /> Anarch and Camarilla Books - But this time, less gay genocide and make it an Actual Useful Book. How do vampires siege cities under the eye of the SI? <br /> <br /> Baali Book - Reveal that Rudi is Tanithbaal-Sahar and that they are taking advantage of the diminished stability to Raise the Children.<br /> <br /> Second Inquisition - Reveal it's the Technocracy considering Vampires a credible threat to Consensus after The Bangladesh Incident of 1999. Secret Vatican drone strikes and cabals of government agents tie in perfectly to the good old Order of Reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>God yes. Or maybe a V5.5/V6? SI as Technocracy stooges feels way more in-keeping with the world we've been playing in for the last three decades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T03:13:26-08:00","id":1428840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1422370-what-books-do-you-want?p=1428839#post1428839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God yes. Or maybe a V5.5/V6? SI as Technocracy stooges feels way more in-keeping with the world we've been playing in for the last three decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Won\u2019t happen. Beyond anything else, they\u2019d only be acting to alienate the existing fans of V5. The time and resources to make a new edition of a major game brand is huge, while other mediums like video games are relying on a degree of continuity from the game\u2019s source too. There has been plenty of disruption already in the last few years, so right now the new development team will be working on new books for the existing game - and let's be clear, the books coming out of Onyx Path especially have been excellent so far. There is plenty of mileage left in this edition. The fan base does not need another edition war.<br /> <br /> When people say things like \u2018fix the mechanics\u2019, they do realize that they are merely expressing individual opinions? For me, the V5 mechanics are the best designed mechanics that the Vampire game has ever had - and there have been lots of reviews that have essentially said the same. Beyond that, I\u2019ve been playing the game since 1991, and V5 is perfectly in line with the original game and intent, however you have chosen to play it for the last three decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T11:11:02-08:00","id":1429962,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I would love if they did for Vampire what &quot;Shattered Dreams&quot; did for Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Just give us &quot;Enoch by Night&quot; and reveal everything. Who sired who, when, who hates who and why, stats for the Antediluvians were they were &quot;just&quot; Elders, etc. People who wouldn't want to see all the secrets revealed could just ignore it as non-canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}